# SteelLab Pro UI Standards

## Square corners

All user-facing surfaces use **square corners** (`border-radius: 0`). No rounded pills, chips, or soft cards.

### Applies to

- Buttons (`.btn`, `.btn-primary`, `.btn-ghost`)
- Inputs, selects, textareas
- Cards, panels, modals, dropdown menus
- Header bar, sidebar nav items, footer areas
- Tables and table wrappers
- Badges, preview panels, auth cards, feature cards
- Avatars and logo marks (square, not circular)

### Implementation

1. **Theme token**: `--radius: 0` in `apps/web/src/app/globals.css`
2. **Tailwind**: `@theme inline` sets `--radius-sm` through `--radius-full` to `0`
3. **CSS classes**: use `border-radius: 0` or `var(--radius)` on shared components
4. **Tailwind utilities**: use `rounded-none` if needed; **never** `rounded-lg`, `rounded-xl`, `rounded-full`, etc.

## AppShell main content padding

All authenticated app pages render inside `AppShell` main content. Padding is **only** on that shell wrapper — not repeated on each page root.

- **Top**: `2mm`
- **Left**: `2mm`
- **Right**: `2mm`
- **Bottom**: none (content scrolls to edge)

```tsx
// AppShell.tsx — single source of truth
<div className="flex-1 pt-[2mm] px-[2mm] overflow-auto">{children}</div>
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — duplicate padding on every page
<div className="space-y-8 p-[2mm]">...</div>

// ✅ GOOD — page root without extra shell padding
<div className="space-y-8 w-full">...</div>
```

Do **not** use `p-8` or large fixed padding on the main content wrapper unless the user explicitly requests a change.

## Copy & language

- App UI text: **English**, Title Case for labels (small words like *of*, *for*, *the* stay lowercase unless first/last).
- Explanations to the user: **Hindi** when requested.
